# Bundled portable Node (Windows-only, ~106 MB): handy locally for building /
# previewing without a separate Node install, but NOT committed — contributors
# install Node themselves, and end users just open MapletViewer.html.
tools/

# Raw downloaded datasets / scratch data used only to GENERATE the sample — too big to
# commit. sample-data/make-merfish-sample.py fetches its data via squidpy; the ~6.2 MB
# tsv it writes (sample-data/merfish-hypothalamus.cells.tsv) IS committed — that's the
# demo dataset users download and open (no longer inlined into the app).
examples/
*.h5ad

# Leftover sample OUTPUTS from abandoned prototypes (07 typed-header, two-row header,
# the solar-system + zhuang demos) — not part of the release. Only the MERFISH sample
# and its generator ship in sample-data/.
sample-data/sample.cells.tsv
sample-data/sample.tworow.cells.tsv
sample-data/solar-system.cells.tsv
sample-data/continuous-test.cells.tsv

# The built single-file app IS committed (MapletViewer.html) so anyone can
# download it and run in a browser; regenerate it with `npm run build:web`.
